        "original_id": "ed745679-15fe-5f67-8e01-79334de38218",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Thiele\n- Places: Thiele Highway, Bower, South Australia, Eudunda, Morgan, Western Australia, South Australia, Victoria, New South Wales\n- Roles: author, educator\n- Topics: highway naming, species distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Milton Thiele was born on 16 November 1920 and died on 4 September 2006.\n- Colin Milton Thiele was an Australian author and educator.\n- Thiele Highway is named after author Colin Thiele.\n- Colin Thiele lived most of his life in towns along Thiele Highway's route and set some of his stories in that area.\n- Bower is a town in South Australia located approximately halfway between Eudunda and Morgan on the Thiele Highway.\n- Bossiaea walkeri occurs in Western Australia, South Australia, Victoria, and New South Wales.",
